      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485058457": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-10T21:21:55.101077+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Description\nWe are seeking a technically strong Distributed Cache & Java Support Engineer to support distributed caching solutions and onboard Java and Spring Boot application use cases to the distributed-cache platform.\nThe candidate will combine hands-on Java development with practical enterprise distributed cache or in-memory data grid experience.\nThe role focuses on cache use-case assessment and onboarding, Java integration support, distributed-cache troubleshooting, and JVM diagnostics.\nKey Responsibilities\nProvide production support for distributed cache clusters and related Java application integrations\nMonitor cluster health, partition distribution, memory, latency, throughput, capacity, and performance\nSupport cache configuration and troubleshooting across distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction and expiry/TTL, partitioning, backup and replication, serialization, and cluster discovery\nDiagnose cache-related incidents including high latency, memory pressure, member restarts, split-brain conditions, data inconsistency, and degraded performance\nCoordinate with application, infrastructure, and vendor support teams to investigate issues and drive technical resolution\nReview and modify Java or Spring Boot code required to onboard application use cases to the distributed-cache platform\nWork with application teams to understand the use case, data model, access pattern, expected load, and caching objectives\nImplement application-side cache integration changes and validate serialization, distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction/TTL, and client configuration\nTroubleshoot JVM and application issues encountered during onboarding, integration testing, and production stabilization\nMinimum Qualification & Experience\nBachelor's degree in computer science, Software Engineering, or Information Technology\n7+ years of relevant experience in Java backend development, Java application support, distributed systems, or closely related engineering work\n3+ years of hands-on experience with distributed caching or in-memory data grid technologies in conjunction with Java applications\nMust Have\nStrong hands-on Java development experience, including the ability to write and modify Java code\nStrong JVM troubleshooting capability, including memory management, garbage collection, thread dumps, heap analysis, and performance diagnosis\nHands-on Spring Boot development or application-support experience, including cache integration or use-case onboarding\nHands-on experience with any distributed caching or in-memory data grid technology such as Redis, Hazelcast, Apache Ignite, Ehcache, Oracle Coherence, Infinispan, Memcached, or comparable platforms. Training will be provided on the selected platform.\nStrong understanding of distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction/expiry/TTL, partitioning, backup/replication, split-brain, serialization, and cluster discovery\nGood to Have\nProduction application support experience in banking, telecom, or other mission-critical environments, including incident triage, root cause analysis, and documentation\nBasic support-level exposure to Kubernetes, containers, Linux, networking, and optionally Anthos or OpenShift; deep platform expertise is not required\nFamiliarity with CI/CD processes and deployment-pipeline troubleshooting\nExperience with Splunk, AppDynamics, or Hazel cast Management Center, plus basic TLS/mTLS and certificate troubleshooting.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486666384": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-10T21:21:55.101077+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates in the technology sector, focusing on developing software solutions that meet project requirements and improve existing systems. It addresses the challenge of building reliable, scalable, and efficient technology by applying strong software development principles and collaborative engineering practices. The organization emphasizes practical software development and continuous learning within a team environment.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE DEVELOPER is responsible for contributing to the development, testing, and maintenance of software applications. This role supports the organization by applying programming knowledge and problem-solving skills to build and enhance software solutions that meet business objectives. It offers an opportunity to work on real-world technical challenges and develop practical software products while growing technical expertise.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop, test, debug, and maintain software applications based on project requirements.\nWrite clean, efficient, reusable, and maintainable code following best practices.\nCollaborate with developers and cross-functional team members to design and implement features.\nUse programming languages such as Python, Java, JavaScript, or TypeScript.\nAssist in developing and integrating REST APIs and web application components.\nWork with databases and SQL to manage application data.\nIdentify and troubleshoot software defects and performance issues.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback.\nUse Git and GitHub for version control.\nWrite and execute unit tests to ensure software reliability.\nDocument technical processes, features, and workflows.\nLearn and apply new tools, frameworks, and technologies.\nRequirements:\nMaster's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or related field.\n0–1 year of experience in Software Engineering, Software Development, or related role.\nStrong understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented programming.\nProficiency in at least one programming language such as Python, Java, JavaScript, or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with data structures and algorithms.\nUnderstanding of REST APIs and web application fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with SQL, relational databases, and basic database concepts.\nExperience using Git and GitHub for version control.\nUnderstanding of software development life cycle principles.\nFamiliarity with debugging, testing, and writing maintainable code.\nStrong analytical thinking and problem-solving abilities.\nAbility to learn new technologies and adapt to project requirements.\nStrong communication, teamwork, and collaboration skills.\nMotivation to build reliable software and continuously improve technical skills.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nAbout the Opportunity (Preferred Qualifications):\nExperience with academic, internship, or personal software development projects.\nFamiliarity with frontend frameworks like React or backend frameworks like Node.js, Django, or Spring Boot.\nBasic knowledge of cloud platforms, software deployment, or CI/CD.\nFamiliarity with Agile development and collaborative workflows.\nOpportunity to work with modern development tools and engineering practices.\nCollaborative environment promoting knowledge sharing and continuous learning.\nOpportunities for professional development and career growth.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487621400": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-10T21:21:55.101077+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Description\nWe are a small SaaS team looking for a Junior Python Developer to build and maintain backend APIs with FastAPI and PostgreSQL, write unit tests, and fix bugs. You will collaborate closely with engineering team members, implement new features, review code, and participate in daily standups to ensure robust and maintainable software delivery.\nResponsibilities\nImplement API endpoints using FastAPI and PostgreSQL\nWrite unit tests and ensure code quality\nFix software bugs and address performance bottlenecks\nReview peer pull requests and collaborate on code architecture\nParticipate actively in daily agile standups\nRequired Skills\nPython\nFastAPI\nPostgreSQL\nGit\nUnit Testing\nPreferred Skills\nDocker\nAmazon Web Services (AWS)\nRESTful APIs\nCI/CD",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488750040": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-10T21:21:55.101077+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. develops technology and solutions that support clinical research, medical imaging, and the documentation of patient outcomes. Our work brings together software, imaging, and clinical expertise to help professionals manage information and make effective use of visual data. We value thoughtful problem-solving, dependable collaboration, and a commitment to quality in the products and services we provide.\nAbout The Role\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. is seeking a Clinical PHP Web Developer, Level I, to contribute to the development and maintenance of web-based applications used in clinical and research environments. This is an opportunity for an early-career developer to strengthen technical skills while working with a focused, creative team. The ideal candidate communicates clearly, takes initiative, manages time effectively, and approaches work with care and curiosity. You will collaborate with colleagues to understand requirements, implement solutions, and help deliver reliable, user-friendly software. A genuine interest in professional growth and contributing to a dynamic group is important for success in this position.\nQualifications\nCandidates should have a foundational understanding of PHP and web application development, along with familiarity with core web technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Experience working with databases and writing or updating SQL queries is helpful. Applicants should be comfortable learning existing code, investigating issues, and asking questions when requirements or technical details are unclear. Strong written and verbal communication skills are essential, as the role involves coordinating with developers and other team members. We are looking for someone who is self-motivated, organized, dependable, and able to balance multiple tasks while meeting agreed timelines. An interest in clinical software, research, or healthcare technology is welcome. Equivalent practical experience, coursework, or personal projects may help demonstrate relevant skills.\nResponsibilities\nAssist in designing, developing, testing, and maintaining PHP-based web applications and related features. Work with team members to clarify user needs and translate defined requirements into practical technical solutions. Review existing application behavior, identify opportunities for improvement, and help troubleshoot defects or performance concerns. Write readable, maintainable code and follow established development practices, documenting changes where appropriate. Support integration with databases and other application components, and help verify that updates work as intended across supported environments. Participate in code reviews, testing, and team discussions to share progress and receive feedback. Communicate risks, questions, and project status promptly. Contribute to the ongoing reliability and usability of clinical web tools, while following applicable internal processes for handling sensitive information. The scope of assignments will reflect a Level I position, with guidance and opportunities to build greater independence over time.\nBenefits\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. offers the opportunity to develop professionally while contributing to meaningful clinical and research technology. Team members can gain hands-on experience with real-world web applications, learn from colleagues across disciplines, and build skills through practical assignments and constructive feedback. Compensation, benefits, and other employment details will be discussed during the hiring process and may vary based on applicable policies and eligibility.\nEqual Opportunity\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. is committed to providing equal employment opportunities. Employment decisions are made without regard to characteristics protected by applicable law. We welcome qualified applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences and are committed to a respectful, inclusive workplace.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T21:21:55.101077+00:00"
  },
